# Maewyn Ashvale - druid of the deep hills (Act 1 sidequest). Sends the guild
# message; recruitable companion.
# Compile with:  scripts\Compile-Dialogue.ps1

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_Maewyn

entry joined if in_party()
entry sent if flag(TSC_MaewynSent)

== start ==
The cottage door opens before you knock. The woman in it has grey-green eyes, a raven on her shoulder, and the expression of someone who knew you were coming but is still unimpressed.

"Boots on my moss. Steel on your hip. And the smell of the guild's ink about you." The raven clicks its beak. "Well. The wind said someone was coming. Speak your business, rider, and mind the beds."

* "Serra Voss's company needs a message carried to the Wayfarers' Guild." -> message
* "Your bees are wintering early. That's a hard-cold sign, this far from frost." -> bees
    if not flag(TSC_MaewynBees)
    check Nature 7 -> bees | bees_miss
* "How did you know I was coming?" -> hills

== bees ==
Maewyn stops. Actually stops, hand on the doorframe, and looks at you properly for the first time.

"...They are. Six weeks early, and the hills won't say why." Her shoulders ease. "A rider who reads bees. Well. Come in, then, properly, and wipe your boots. Whatever your business is, it just got easier to hear."

* "The business is a message for the guild." -> message
    do flag(TSC_MaewynBees); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)

== bees_miss ==
Maewyn follows your gesture to the hives and snorts.

"That's not wintering, rider, that's *sulking*. I moved their south board on Tuesday. Kind of you to notice bees exist, though. Most of your sort only notice the honey."

* "Then I'll get to my business: a message for the guild." -> message

== hills ==
"The hills talk, if you've the patience to be quiet longer than they are. Eight weeks they've muttered about the crownhunters in the pass, and three days about the new rider poking the old places awake."

She steps back from the door, which is as close to an invitation as you suspect she gives.

"You're the rider. So: the crownhunters finally need something. Out with it."

* "A message to the guild. They lost their raven." -> message

== message ==
"Lost their raven." The one on her shoulder clicks its beak, and Maewyn's mouth twitches; on anyone else it would be a smile. "Corvus heard. He's insufferable about hawks."

She considers you for a long, unhurried moment.

"I'll send your message, rider. Not for the guild (guilds are just villages that learned to walk) but because Serra Voss once turned her whole company sideways to keep a fire off my grove, and debts between neighbors matter."

She holds out a hand for the letter.

* "Here. The guild will know the party lives." -> agreed
* [Insight] "This grove is lonely, Maewyn. Even with the ravens." -> lonely
    if passive(Insight, 8)

== agreed ==
Maewyn signals a nearby raven, ties the message with a strip of bark-cord, murmurs something to the raven that is definitely not any language you know, and casts it into the sky.

"Done. My birds fly faster than any rider; the guild will read it inside a week."

She watches the bird shrink to a speck.

"If you'd take some advice: when the ettersnap speaks, listen to what it *doesn't* say."

* "How did you know about the ettersnap?" -> ettersnap
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent)
* "Come with me. We could use your help." -> recruit
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent)
* "Thank you, Maewyn. And the advice is noted." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent)

== ettersnap ==

"My birds are smarter than they look, and they watch and listen."

* "Come with me. We could use your help." -> recruit
* "Thank you, Maewyn. I'll leave you to your bees and birds." -> end

== lonely ==
The raven goes very still. So does Maewyn.

"...The hills talk," she says at last, quieter. "But they don't *answer*. You've a sharp eye, rider." She takes the letter from your hand without ceremony. "I'll send your message. And I'll think about the other thing you didn't quite ask."

* "Then ask it plainly I shall: ride with me, Maewyn." -> recruit
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent); affinity(+5)
* "Thank you, Maewyn." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynSent); signal(TSC_Side_Druid, TSC_MessageSent); affinity(+5)

== recruit ==
Maewyn looks at her grove (the beds, the hives, the mossy quiet) for a long moment.

"Thirty years I've kept this hollow. The hills will keep it thirty more without me." She whistles; the second raven drops from the eaves to her shoulder. "Very well, rider. The grove-cat hunts for herself, the bees answer to nobody, and I... apparently answer to you. Try to deserve it."

* "Welcome to the company, Maewyn." -> welcomed
    do join_party(); affinity(+5)
* "Take a day to be sure. I'll return." -> end

== welcomed ==
She pulls the door shut behind her without locking it and falls in beside you.

"Now. Tell me about this hunt of Serra's."

* "This way, Maewyn."

== sent ==
Maewyn is in her garden, unsurprised as ever.

"The raven is away with your message, rider. Was there something else? Or has the road finally taught you to visit without wanting?"

* "The offer stands: ride with me." -> recruit
* "Just passing. Peace on your grove." -> end

== joined ==
Maewyn is watching the horizon the way other people read.

"The hills are quieter here. I don't trust it. What do you need, rider?"

* "I wouldn't mind learning a thing or two from you." -> druid_teaching
    if not flag(TSC_MaewynTaught)
* "How fares the grove without its keeper?" -> grove_talk
    if affinity(>=10) and not flag(TSC_MaewynGroveTalk)
* "About your cellar, Maewyn..." -> cellar_caught
    if flag(TSC_MaewynCellarTheft) and not flag(TSC_MaewynCellarAired)
* "Carry on, Maewyn."

== cellar_caught ==
Maewyn doesn't look at you. Corvus does, unblinking.

"Thirty years, rider. That lock has kept out storms, wolves, and two kings' tax collectors. It couldn't keep out my own company." She lets the silence do its work. "The book you may keep; knowledge should be shared - you could've just asked. The trust will take longer to restock than the shelf."

* "It won't happen again, Maewyn." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynCellarAired)
* "The company's supplies are the company's business." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynCellarAired); affinity(-5)

== grove_talk ==
Maewyn is quiet long enough that you think she won't answer.

"The grove-cat has the run of it. The bees will sulk and thrive. And the door isn't locked, because a locked door in the hills is a dare." Corvus shifts on her shoulder. "It fares, rider. Thank you for asking, which nobody does."

* "We'll walk you back someday, Maewyn." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynGroveTalk); grant_xp(10)

== druid_teaching ==
"I'm glad you realized I have something to teach." She settles onto a stone as if she'd picked it out an hour ago. "Good. Sit. The first lesson is sitting."

That evening, and for several after, she teaches: how to sit until the birds forget you; which silences mean weather and which mean wolves; what the green things say under the soil, and what they'll say to you.

* [Learn the Druid's way] "I hear it now. Faintly." -> end
    if not flag(TSC_MaewynTaught)
    do flag(TSC_MaewynTaught); learn_class(TSC_Class_Druid); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)
* "This is... a lot of sitting, Maewyn." -> end
